Hi,

you might find this Grid function convenient to display a data.frame,

library(gridExtra) # http://code.google.com/p/gridextra/
grid.table(as.data.frame(round(beta1,3)), cols=expression(beta[1]))

It could be adapted into a geom for ggplot2 (restricted to use with annotate).
